WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.294
Machine learning promises to accelerate therapeutic
antibody design,

00:00:04.374 --> 00:00:09.570
but only if models can accurately read the
sequence-to-function fitness landscape.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.751
This paper introduces FLAb, the Fitness Landscape
for Antibodies,

00:00:13.831 --> 00:00:17.032
the largest therapeutic antibody benchmark to date.

00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:22.629
It gathers experimental measurements for six
developability properties and uses them to

00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:28.225
stress-test six widely used deep learning protein
models against physics-based Rosetta.

00:00:28.305 --> 00:00:34.015
The headline finding is sobering: no single model
correlates well with all six properties,

00:00:34.095 --> 00:00:38.389
and performance swings sharply across datasets of
the same property,

00:00:38.469 --> 00:00:41.220
revealing how far the field still has to go.
